  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "Can you switch financial advisors?",
      "answer": "Yes, you can legally switch financial advisors at any time. Your ability to terminate the relationship and the required notice period depend on the specific terms negotiated in your written advisory contract."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is it hard to switch financial advisors?",
      "answer": "Switching is generally a straightforward administrative process when handled through automated systems. By completing a Transfer Initiation Form with your new receiving firm, most broker-dealer accounts move directly through ACATS in about three to four business days without requiring you to manage individual sales."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does it cost money to switch financial advisors?",
      "answer": "Regulatory guidance publishes no standard fee to switch financial advisors. Your total cost depends entirely on your specific advisory agreement, any contractual termination provisions, and whether the delivering or receiving institutions charge account transfer fees."
    },
    {
      "question": "What happens when you switch financial advisors?",
      "answer": "When you switch, your receiving firm requests your assets from your old firm using a Transfer Initiation Form. Your positions move through an automated transfer service like ACATS, after which your new adviser takes over portfolio monitoring and management."
    }
  ],
